title: b1.1 Mindful Walk
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Eight values. Social connectedness leads: company is the reason to walk and to talk. Dignity includes face: a slip is not exposed. Truthfulness: the System does not deceive, corrects its own errors, and leaves painful truths to a trusted person. Privacy covers other people's secrets as well as one's own.

= Human Value - Autonomy [HV-01] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-01
|Name|Autonomy
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|Walk or not, with whom, how long. Choose own settings. Consent before joining a person and before each conversation starter.
|Held by|ST-01, ST-02 (high); ST-05 (medium)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Intrinsic. Also supports Dignity.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: the resident sets and changes their own settings; a "no" ends the offer, without a reason asked.

Violated: walks arranged for staff convenience; a starter used without asking; persuasion; reminders of missed walks.
)))
|Source|Ryan, R. M. & Deci, E. L. (2000). Self-determination theory and the facilitation of intrinsic motivation, social development, and well-being. //American Psychologist//, 55(1), 68-78.

= Human Value - Dignity [HV-02] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-02
|Name|Dignity
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|Spoken to as an adult. Slips are not remarked on. No quizzing, no correcting, no praise for walking. A walk taken for the resident's sake, never as a routine run.
|Held by|ST-01 (high); ST-02 (medium)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Intrinsic.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: help after a slip offered to both walkers, as a statement; the slip not mentioned afterwards.

Violated: "You told me that already"; "Do you remember...?"; finishing someone's sentence; being "taken out" like a dog.
)))
|Source|Kitwood, T. (1997). //Dementia Reconsidered: The Person Comes First//. Open University Press. Goffman, E. (1967). //Interaction Ritual//. Anchor Books.

= Human Value - Privacy [HV-03] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-03
|Name|Privacy
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|(((
Own conversations, own secrets, own whereabouts. Another resident's secrets never reach you through the System. Data stays in the care home.

Staff: no surveillance of their own work.
)))
|Held by|ST-01, ST-02, ST-05, ST-07 (high); ST-04, ST-06 (medium); ST-03 (low - may want more than the resident would share)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Intrinsic. Also supports Dignity.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: nothing leaves the home; only consented items exchanged; no audio stored.

Violated: a secret said to the wrong person; conversation recorded; route logged.
)))
|Source|Friedman, B., Kahn, P. H., Jr. & Borning, A. (2008). Value Sensitive Design and Information Systems. Niemeijer, A. R. et al. (2010). Ethical and practical concerns of surveillance technologies in residential care for people with dementia or intellectual disabilities. //International Psychogeriatrics//.

= Human Value - Safety [HV-04] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-04
|Name|Safety
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|No falls, no getting lost; help arrives quickly. Talking while walking raises the risk.
|Held by|ST-04, ST-06, ST-07 (high); ST-01 (medium)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Instrumental: the condition for walking at all.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: stumbles and tiredness noticed; alerts reach a person.

Violated: the walk continues past tiredness; a fall goes unanswered.
)))
|Source|Härlein, J. et al. (2009). Fall risk factors in older people with dementia or cognitive impairment. //Journal of Advanced Nursing//, 65(5), 922-933. Lundin-Olsson et al. (1997).

= Human Value - Well-being [HV-05] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-05
|Name|Well-being
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|Fresh air, movement, calm. Emotional safety: free from embarrassment, conflict, pressure, and painful news at the wrong moment.
|Held by|ST-01 to ST-04, ST-06 (high); ST-07 (medium)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Intrinsic.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: pleasure on the walk; calm afterwards.

Violated: distress after a slip, a clash or a blunt answer.
)))
|Source|Forbes, D. et al. (2015). Exercise programs for people with dementia. //Cochrane Database of Systematic Reviews//, (4), CD006489. Bratman et al. (2015).

= Human Value - Social connectedness [HV-06] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-06
|Name|Social connectedness
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|Company and conversation: a fellow resident, or the guide where agreed. Less lonely.
|Held by|ST-01, ST-02, ST-03, ST-05 (high)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Both. Valued in itself; also the reason to go out.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: more walks with company; conversations resume after slips.

Violated: a device in place of people; partners withdraw after slips.
)))
|Source|Victor, C. R. (2012). Loneliness in care homes: a neglected area of research? //Aging Health//, 8(6), 637-646. Holwerda et al. (2014).

= Human Value - Identity [HV-07] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-07
|Name|Identity
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|Remain who you were: trade, places, people, own words and dialect.
|Held by|ST-01, ST-03, ST-05 (high)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Intrinsic. Also gives conversation a subject.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: starters from the resident's own life, in their own words.

Violated: wrong facts about one's life; generic content.
)))
|Source|Kitwood (1997). Woods, B. et al. (2018). Reminiscence therapy for dementia. //Cochrane Database of Systematic Reviews//, (3), CD001120.

= Human Value - Truthfulness [HV-08] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-08
|Name|Truthfulness
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|(((
No deception by design: no lies, kind ones included; no denials; no playing along with an untrue belief. Trust once lost is rarely regained.

Errors cannot be ruled out: the System mishears, a profile can be out of date, a resident's own words can be mistaken. So it states facts only from checked sources, attributes what others said, says less when unsure, and corrects itself plainly when contradicted.

Painful truths (a death, a diagnosis) come from a trusted person, never from the System.
)))
|Held by|ST-01, ST-03, ST-04, ST-06 (high)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Intrinsic. Also instrumental: trust is the condition for accepting any help.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: no untruth, denial or playing along in the script; errors corrected at once and fixed at their source; sensitive questions passed to the trusted person; one agreed answer across staff.

Violated: "He's at work"; an error left standing; the guide states a death; different answers from different people.
)))
|Source|Mental Health Foundation (2016). //What Is Truth?// James et al. (2006).

